1
00:01:57,571 --> 00:02:02,075
Marcus.

2
00:02:06,246 --> 00:02:08,664
How are you?

3
00:02:08,665 --> 00:02:13,169
Ask me in an hour.

4
00:02:13,628 --> 00:02:16,004
I thought I'd try...

5
00:02:16,005 --> 00:02:18,423
...one last time.

6
00:02:18,424 --> 00:02:22,929
You should have stayed
in San Francisco, Dr. Kogan.

7
00:02:24,263 --> 00:02:26,181
By signing this consent form...

8
00:02:26,182 --> 00:02:30,351
...you'd be donating your body
to a noble cause.

9
00:02:30,352 --> 00:02:32,562
You'd...

10
00:02:32,563 --> 00:02:38,444
...have a second chance,
through my research, to live again.

11
00:02:38,610 --> 00:02:41,070
You know what I did.

12
00:02:41,071 --> 00:02:44,740
My brother and two cops are dead
because of me.

13
00:02:44,741 --> 00:02:49,246
I'm not looking for a second chance.

14
00:02:52,165 --> 00:02:56,669
But I'm not the only one
with a death sentence, am I?

15
00:02:58,129 --> 00:03:02,633
Do you think
I'm gonna cure your cancer, Serena?

16
00:03:02,675 --> 00:03:06,553
I'm not worried about myself.

17
00:03:06,554 --> 00:03:11,058
I'm worried about the future
of the human race.

18
00:03:11,475 --> 00:03:14,644
I'll sell it to you.

19
00:03:14,645 --> 00:03:16,646
For what?

20
00:03:16,647 --> 00:03:21,151
A kiss.

21
00:03:24,863 --> 00:03:29,367
Mm.

22
00:03:31,536 --> 00:03:34,997
Oh...

23
00:03:34,998 --> 00:03:39,502
So that's what death tastes like.

24
00:03:55,142 --> 00:03:57,935
You're doing something very noble.

25
00:03:57,936 --> 00:03:59,729
No, I'm guilty.

26
00:03:59,730 --> 00:04:04,234
Just cut me up
until there's nothing left.

27
00:04:06,403 --> 00:04:10,907
PRIEST: Yea, though I walk through
the valley of the shadow of death...

28
00:04:11,116 --> 00:04:15,577
...I will fear no evil,
for thou art with me.

29
00:04:15,578 --> 00:04:20,083
Thy rod and thy staff,
they comfort me.

30
00:04:34,179 --> 00:04:38,684
Do you have any last words?

31
00:06:09,521 --> 00:06:11,481
MAN
Vanguard, this is Blackjack 6.

32
00:06:11,482 --> 00:06:13,232
Missile inbound to Skynet target.

33
00:06:13,233 --> 00:06:17,695
TTO 11 seconds. Danger close.

34
00:06:49,976 --> 00:06:54,481
Move! Move!
Let's go, let's go! Move it!

35
00:07:04,824 --> 00:07:09,328
MAN 2
Connor is on the ground.

36
00:07:10,746 --> 00:07:12,581
This mission is a quick in-and-out.

37
00:07:12,582 --> 00:07:15,249
Command deems the information
on those computers...

38
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:19,755
...to be of the highest priority.

39
00:07:49,617 --> 00:07:52,202
BARBAROSA
Connor, there's no sign of the machines.

40
00:07:52,203 --> 00:07:53,453
They're gone.

41
00:07:53,454 --> 00:07:54,872
DAVID
It's way too quiet.

42
00:07:54,873 --> 00:07:59,376
BARBAROSA
It's almost like they're waiting for us.

43
00:08:04,923 --> 00:08:09,427
SOLDIER:
It's down, it's down.

44
00:08:29,822 --> 00:08:32,156
DAVID
What the hell's that smell, man?

45
00:08:32,157 --> 00:08:33,825
Ugh.

46
00:08:33,826 --> 00:08:38,330
JOHN
You seeing this?

47
00:08:58,266 --> 00:09:02,018
Olsen. Objective located.

48
00:09:02,019 --> 00:09:06,524
There's something else
you have to see.

49
00:09:22,748 --> 00:09:25,082
Hard wall.
Get what we came for, Barbarosa.

50
00:09:25,083 --> 00:09:26,542
The clock's ticking.

51
00:09:26,543 --> 00:09:29,753
Spread out, secure the perimeter.
I got a big gap over here.

52
00:09:29,754 --> 00:09:33,173
Why didn't we know about this?

53
00:09:33,174 --> 00:09:35,051
Sir, I think this is
what Command's looking for.

54
00:09:35,052 --> 00:09:36,885
I'm in their source code.

55
00:09:36,886 --> 00:09:39,304
These people are being taken
to San Francisco.

56
00:09:39,305 --> 00:09:42,099
Some sort of R and D project
for a new Terminator.

57
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:44,184
Send it to Command.

58
00:09:44,185 --> 00:09:45,645
It's uploading. I need two minutes.

59
00:09:45,646 --> 00:09:48,396
Wait, wait, wait.
Go back. Go back.

60
00:09:48,397 --> 00:09:52,902
Stop.

61
00:09:54,486 --> 00:09:58,948
T-800.
A new Terminator.

62
00:09:58,949 --> 00:10:01,117
It's like you said it would be.

63
00:10:01,118 --> 00:10:03,953
- It's worse.
Get your nose out of that.

64
00:10:03,954 --> 00:10:06,747
None of your business.
You're not leading this mission.

65
00:10:06,748 --> 00:10:09,917
Let's cut these sorry bastards loose.
Come on. Let's go.

66
00:10:09,918 --> 00:10:12,252
- Jericho, come in.
Watch that.

67
00:10:12,253 --> 00:10:13,921
Come in, Jericho.

68
00:10:13,922 --> 00:10:16,632
Connor, get your ass topside.
Remind those men...

69
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:20,093
...they need to answer me on the radio,
even if they're dead.

70
00:10:20,094 --> 00:10:24,599
Connor!

71
00:10:33,274 --> 00:10:35,109
OLSEN
Connor, get those men to respond.

72
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:39,613
Olsen, something's wrong up here.

73
00:10:48,455 --> 00:10:52,959
OLSEN
Topside, come in.

74
00:10:53,376 --> 00:10:57,880
Outbound enemy aircraft.
I'm in pursuit.

75
00:10:58,256 --> 00:11:02,760
There's human prisoners
aboard that thing. Get after it!

76
00:11:18,317 --> 00:11:20,067
OLSEN
Data transfer complete.

77
00:11:20,068 --> 00:11:24,573
Connor, we're joining you topsi-

78
00:12:04,694 --> 00:12:09,199
Olsen.

79
00:13:03,459 --> 00:13:07,963
MAN Bravo 10,
Bravo 10, do you copy? Over.

80
00:13:11,008 --> 00:13:15,512
Eagle 1 to Bravo 10.
Bravo 10, do you copy? Over.

81
00:13:17,765 --> 00:13:22,269
Bravo 10, Bravo 10,
do you copy? Over?

82
00:13:23,979 --> 00:13:25,438
Here.

83
00:13:25,439 --> 00:13:28,524
MAN
Bravo 10, identify. Over.

84
00:13:28,525 --> 00:13:29,900
Connor.

85
00:13:29,901 --> 00:13:31,611
MAN
We'll send units to the extraction point.

86
00:13:31,612 --> 00:13:34,029
How many survivors are on-site? Over.

87
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:36,615
One.

88
00:13:36,616 --> 00:13:41,120
MAN
Copy.

89
00:14:43,847 --> 00:14:46,558
PILOT:
Return to base, sir?

90
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:49,019
- RTB?
- Negative.

91
00:14:49,060 --> 00:14:53,063
- Take me to Command.
- Sir?

92
00:14:53,064 --> 00:14:55,400
Command.

93
00:14:55,441 --> 00:14:59,904
Roger. Rerouting.

94
00:15:16,086 --> 00:15:17,379
PILOT:
Request has been denied.

95
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:20,840
Command doesn't wanna give up
their position. Radio comms only.

96
00:15:20,841 --> 00:15:24,260
- Are they down there?
- Request has been denied, sir.

97
00:15:24,261 --> 00:15:28,723
Need-to-know only.
That's straight from the top.

98
00:15:29,683 --> 00:15:31,934
You open up that ramp...

99
00:15:31,935 --> 00:15:37,815
...and you tell them I need divers for
a lock-in! Now!

100
00:15:40,276 --> 00:15:44,739
PILOT:
This is crazy.

101
00:16:09,846 --> 00:16:11,472
John Connor.

102
00:16:11,473 --> 00:16:14,099
Prophesized leader
of the Resistance.

103
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:17,227
Soldier, you put every man and woman
in this sub in jeopardy...

104
00:16:17,228 --> 00:16:19,813
...with your little frogman stunt.

105
00:16:19,814 --> 00:16:23,650
Let's get one thing straight.

106
00:16:23,651 --> 00:16:27,654
I don't believe in prophecy.

107
00:16:27,655 --> 00:16:32,243
Not when one can rewrite
the future in a heartbeat.

108
00:16:32,409 --> 00:16:36,914
Are we on the same page?

109
00:16:37,664 --> 00:16:42,169
Yeah, we're on the same page.

110
00:16:43,879 --> 00:16:48,383
Good. Good.

111
00:16:49,718 --> 00:16:51,635
So, soldier...

112
00:16:51,636 --> 00:16:53,762
...what the hell are you doing here?

113
00:16:53,763 --> 00:16:56,598
- What did we find down there?
- You'll be briefed...

114
00:16:56,599 --> 00:16:59,226
- ... on a need-to-know basis.
- Well, I need to know.

115
00:16:59,227 --> 00:17:02,437
Because my men died
down in that hole.

116
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:04,314
What did we find down there?

117
00:17:04,315 --> 00:17:10,529
We found a solution, Connor,
that can end this war once and for all.

118
00:17:13,032 --> 00:17:17,326
We know the machines use shortwave
transmitters to communicate.

119
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:21,832
Intel has located a hidden signal
under the primary channel.

120
00:17:22,165 --> 00:17:25,584
It allows for direct control
of the machines.

121
00:17:25,585 --> 00:17:28,212
Skynet's a machine,
and like all machines...

122
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:31,215
...it has an off switch.

123
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:32,674
Does it work?

124
00:17:32,675 --> 00:17:37,263
Will it work? Yes.
Have we field tested it? No.

125
00:17:38,222 --> 00:17:41,016
Give it to me.

126
00:17:41,017 --> 00:17:42,893
I'll do it.

127
00:17:42,894 --> 00:17:47,063
I'll test it.

128
00:17:47,064 --> 00:17:50,859
Connor and his tech-comm unit
have an excellent record.

129
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:53,570
All right.

130
00:17:53,571 --> 00:17:56,280
All right. Huh.

131
00:17:56,281 --> 00:18:00,786
Take Connor topside.
Prepare for lockout.

132
00:18:04,122 --> 00:18:08,584
Connor, we do this right,
the war is over.

133
00:18:08,585 --> 00:18:13,089
We mount our offensive in four days.

134
00:18:14,257 --> 00:18:17,509
Connor.

135
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:20,887
These are the codes for the signal.

136
00:18:20,888 --> 00:18:23,640
- Good luck.
- Why four days?

137
00:18:23,641 --> 00:18:26,309
A kill list was intercepted
from Skynet.

138
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:29,854
It says everyone in this room
will be dead by week's end.

139
00:18:29,855 --> 00:18:33,441
You're number two on the list.

140
00:18:33,442 --> 00:18:39,239
- Well, who's number one?
- An unknown. A civilian. Kyle Reese.

141
00:19:09,894 --> 00:19:12,645
OLSEN
Jericho, come in.

142
00:19:12,646 --> 00:19:17,151
Come in, Jericho.

143
00:19:19,194 --> 00:19:23,699
Barnes.

144
00:19:23,865 --> 00:19:28,370
My brother,
he didn't make it, did he?

145
00:20:15,582 --> 00:20:19,835
This is tape number 28
of Sarah Connor to my son, John.

146
00:20:19,836 --> 00:20:22,087
What's most difficult
is trying to decide...

147
00:20:22,088 --> 00:20:24,756
...what to tell you and what not to.

148
00:20:24,757 --> 00:20:26,800
Should I tell you about your father?

149
00:20:26,801 --> 00:20:30,845
Will it affect your decision to
send him back in time to protect me...

150
00:20:30,846 --> 00:20:33,097
...knowing that he is your father?

151
00:20:33,098 --> 00:20:36,476
And he'll be younger than you.
Only a teenager when you meet him.

152
00:20:36,477 --> 00:20:39,937
God, a person could go crazy
thinking about this.

153
00:20:39,938 --> 00:20:43,149
But if you don't send Kyle,
you can never be...

154
00:20:43,150 --> 00:20:47,654
...and Skynet will win the war.

155
00:20:49,698 --> 00:20:53,325
You want to talk about him?

156
00:20:53,326 --> 00:20:58,164
Kyle is out there somewhere alone,
and Skynet is hunting him.

157
00:20:58,873 --> 00:21:01,833
What about the signal?

158
00:21:01,834 --> 00:21:06,339
What do you think?

159
00:21:12,303 --> 00:21:15,054
If it works, it's incredible.
Yeah.

160
00:21:15,055 --> 00:21:17,557
We have to be careful.
- I agree.

161
00:21:17,558 --> 00:21:21,143
- But we have to try.
Okay.

162
00:21:21,144 --> 00:21:25,649
All right, start with something small
that we're familiar with.

163
00:21:27,692 --> 00:21:31,236
We should capture a Hydrobot,
bring it in for testing.

164
00:21:31,237 --> 00:21:33,906
Yeah.

165
00:21:33,907 --> 00:21:38,035
What is it, John?

166
00:21:38,036 --> 00:21:42,540
Kill Kyle Reese, reset the future...

167
00:21:42,748 --> 00:21:47,253
...no John Connor.

168
00:22:24,205 --> 00:22:28,709
Hey!

169
00:23:08,372 --> 00:23:12,877
Come with me if you wanna live.

170
00:24:15,061 --> 00:24:17,771
What is that?

171
00:24:17,772 --> 00:24:21,483
She doesn't talk,
but you need to start.

172
00:24:21,484 --> 00:24:23,235
Where'd you get that jacket?

173
00:24:23,236 --> 00:24:26,154
- The other guy didn't need it.
- Oh?

174
00:24:26,155 --> 00:24:27,822
You see that red?

175
00:24:27,823 --> 00:24:30,825
It stands for blood.
It's a symbol of the Resistance.

176
00:24:30,826 --> 00:24:35,289
You're obviously not
a Resistance fighter, so take it off.

177
00:24:35,956 --> 00:24:38,374
Take it off!

178
00:24:38,375 --> 00:24:40,084
You point a gun at someone...

179
00:24:40,085 --> 00:24:44,548
...you'd better be ready
to pull the trigger.

180
00:24:46,716 --> 00:24:50,469
Now, I'm gonna ask you
one more time.

181
00:24:50,470 --> 00:24:53,388
- What the hell was that thing?
- Terminator.

182
00:24:53,389 --> 00:24:57,852
T-600.

183
00:24:58,895 --> 00:25:01,730
What day is it?

184
00:25:01,731 --> 00:25:05,650
What year?

185
00:25:05,651 --> 00:25:10,029
2018.

186
00:25:10,030 --> 00:25:14,242
What happened here?

187
00:25:14,243 --> 00:25:18,747
Judgment Day happened.

188
00:25:20,082 --> 00:25:22,291
I gotta get out of here.

189
00:25:22,292 --> 00:25:25,544
You can't go on foot.
The machines will cut you down.

190
00:25:25,545 --> 00:25:27,505
You need speed.

191
00:25:27,506 --> 00:25:28,881
I need a car.

192
00:25:28,882 --> 00:25:32,009
Well, look, there's some
by Griffith Observatory.

193
00:25:32,010 --> 00:25:35,846
- They don't run though.
- Take me.

194
00:25:35,847 --> 00:25:40,351
Get down!

195
00:26:06,626 --> 00:26:10,129
That was a Hunter-Killer.

196
00:26:10,130 --> 00:26:14,634
Thanks to you, they know we're here.

197
00:26:14,926 --> 00:26:17,552
What's your name, kid?

198
00:26:17,553 --> 00:26:22,058
Kyle Reese.

199
00:26:23,059 --> 00:26:25,727
Come on.

200
00:26:25,728 --> 00:26:26,979
WHIRRING AND SQUEALING]

201
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:30,523
We burned out his transmitter
so it can't talk to any of its pals.

202
00:26:30,524 --> 00:26:32,942
But he can still receive.

203
00:26:32,943 --> 00:26:36,487
Turn it on.

204
00:26:36,488 --> 00:26:38,239
You got it?

205
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:42,618
Hold it down, hold it down.

206
00:26:42,619 --> 00:26:47,123
Turn the signal up.

207
00:26:54,672 --> 00:26:56,757
Give me the strap.

208
00:26:56,758 --> 00:27:00,010
- Holy shit.
- Do you believe it?

209
00:27:00,011 --> 00:27:03,305
All right. Strap it tight.
The signal has to be continuous.

210
00:27:03,306 --> 00:27:07,810
If there's any interruption...

211
00:27:09,979 --> 00:27:14,190
JOHN
Okay.

212
00:27:14,191 --> 00:27:18,027
Let's rig up a portable shortwave,
test it on something larger in the field.

213
00:27:18,028 --> 00:27:21,572
All right.

214
00:27:21,573 --> 00:27:26,077
Destroy this thing.

215
00:27:34,419 --> 00:27:35,919
So where are the cars?

216
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:38,171
You don't wanna go out after dark.

217
00:27:38,172 --> 00:27:42,551
Hunter-Killers have infrared,
hunt better at night.

218
00:27:42,552 --> 00:27:47,056
We'll all go tomorrow morning.

219
00:27:49,016 --> 00:27:53,520
What is that?
Two-day-old coyote.

220
00:27:54,396 --> 00:27:58,901
Better than three-day-old coyote.

221
00:28:07,367 --> 00:28:08,617
Hey, hey!

222
00:28:08,618 --> 00:28:13,123
Shhh.

223
00:28:14,124 --> 00:28:16,959
Grab it.
- What?

224
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:21,464
Grab it.

225
00:28:27,470 --> 00:28:31,974
Magic.

226
00:28:33,976 --> 00:28:37,145
Got it?
Yeah.

227
00:28:37,146 --> 00:28:41,650
Thanks.

228
00:28:42,818 --> 00:28:44,860
Does this radio work?

229
00:28:44,861 --> 00:28:46,946
No.

230
00:28:46,947 --> 00:28:51,451
My dad tried to fix it,
but he could never get it to work.

231
00:29:07,842 --> 00:29:12,346
Hold that.

232
00:29:14,765 --> 00:29:16,849
Where is everybody?

233
00:29:16,850 --> 00:29:19,352
They're gone.

234
00:29:19,353 --> 00:29:20,937
So why are you still here?

235
00:29:20,938 --> 00:29:24,023
Because we're the Resistance,
L. A. branch.

236
00:29:24,024 --> 00:29:27,359
Welcome to the headquarters.

237
00:29:27,360 --> 00:29:30,279
Resisting what?

238
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:33,615
Machines. Skynet.

239
00:29:33,616 --> 00:29:37,744
- Just the two of you?
Yeah.

240
00:29:37,745 --> 00:29:40,956
How come you're not
wearing one of these?

241
00:29:40,957 --> 00:29:45,461
Because I haven't earned mine yet.

242
00:29:53,552 --> 00:29:58,056
I hope he's listening to this.

243
00:29:58,557 --> 00:30:00,391
We've been fighting a long time...

244
00:30:00,392 --> 00:30:04,896
...and we have all lost so very much,
so many loved ones gone.

245
00:30:05,063 --> 00:30:07,106
But you are not alone.

246
00:30:07,107 --> 00:30:10,526
There are pockets of Resistance
all around the planet.

247
00:30:10,527 --> 00:30:13,862
We are at the brink.

248
00:30:13,863 --> 00:30:18,368
Do you wanna see a magic trick?
Hold that up.

249
00:30:20,995 --> 00:30:25,499
Press the button.

250
00:30:26,876 --> 00:30:30,712
JOHN Effective range of their
main weapon is less than 100 meters.

251
00:30:30,713 --> 00:30:34,716
They pack a lot of firepower,
but the T-600s are heavy and slow.

252
00:30:34,717 --> 00:30:36,592
They are a primitive design.

253
00:30:36,593 --> 00:30:38,761
- Who is that?
If you can't outrun them...

254
00:30:38,762 --> 00:30:41,222
- I don't know.
- ... then you have one option.

255
00:30:41,223 --> 00:30:44,975
Their motor cortex is partially
exposed at the back of their neck.

256
00:30:44,976 --> 00:30:49,481
A knife to this area will disorient
their tracking device, but not for long.

257
00:30:49,981 --> 00:30:53,067
Above all, stay alive.
You have no idea...

258
00:30:53,068 --> 00:30:57,572
...how important you are,
and how important you will become.

259
00:30:57,697 --> 00:31:01,199
The machines are advancing
even faster than I told you they would.

260
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:02,826
I've seen it with my own eyes.

261
00:31:02,827 --> 00:31:07,163
They're inventing new Terminators,
new ways of killing us.

262
00:31:07,164 --> 00:31:10,291
Skynet is planning something big.

263
00:31:10,292 --> 00:31:14,797
But the Resistance
is planning something bigger.

264
00:31:15,297 --> 00:31:17,090
This is John Connor.

265
00:31:17,091 --> 00:31:21,595
If you're listening to this,
you are the Resistance.

266
00:31:22,929 --> 00:31:26,432
John Connor.

267
00:31:26,433 --> 00:31:30,937
We gotta find this guy.

268
00:31:46,911 --> 00:31:51,415
Ow.

269
00:32:01,174 --> 00:32:05,177
So you get it working?
Almost.

270
00:32:05,178 --> 00:32:09,056
Good. Look,
I figure we head east, right?

271
00:32:09,057 --> 00:32:13,519
We go through the desert, then we can
connect with the Resistance there.

272
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:16,772
- I'm heading north.
No, no, no.

273
00:32:16,773 --> 00:32:20,317
The machines control the whole
northern sector, up to San Francisco.

274
00:32:20,318 --> 00:32:22,778
- That's Skynet Central.
- I have to find someone.

275
00:32:22,779 --> 00:32:25,739
There's a lot you don't understand
about Skynet, okay?

276
00:32:25,740 --> 00:32:29,993
It's just too dangerous for us
to go there.

277
00:32:29,994 --> 00:32:34,498
What about the L. A. branch?

278
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:41,505
Come on, man.
We need to get out of L. A.

279
00:33:02,191 --> 00:33:04,860
What is that?

280
00:33:04,902 --> 00:33:09,365
Something my brother
used to listen to.

281
00:33:12,701 --> 00:33:16,788
Star, get out.

282
00:33:16,789 --> 00:33:19,500
Don't look at me like that, Star.

283
00:33:19,541 --> 00:33:24,004
Out. Get out!

284
00:33:24,212 --> 00:33:28,675
You're leaving?
You're gonna leave us?

285
00:33:29,551 --> 00:33:33,846
Oh, I get it.

286
00:33:33,847 --> 00:33:38,016
You wanna know the difference
between us and the machines?

287
00:33:38,017 --> 00:33:41,478
We bury our dead.

288
00:33:41,479 --> 00:33:45,942
But no one is coming to bury you.

289
00:33:53,741 --> 00:33:54,991
WHIRRING]

290
00:33:54,992 --> 00:33:57,452
Aerostat!

291
00:33:57,453 --> 00:34:01,915
- It's a scout for the Terminators.
- Go, drive!

292
00:34:09,005 --> 00:34:13,510
The Aerostats heard the music!

293
00:34:13,551 --> 00:34:18,056
- Keep it steady!
- I've never driven before.

294
00:34:19,932 --> 00:34:24,437
Hold the wheel!

295
00:34:28,149 --> 00:34:32,653
This thing's pissing me off!

296
00:34:38,158 --> 00:34:39,909
Kid!

297
00:34:39,910 --> 00:34:44,414
Hold on!

298
00:34:56,342 --> 00:35:00,847
If the idea is to stay alive,
I'm driving.

299
00:35:04,642 --> 00:35:08,645
We're seeing a lot
of enemy movement in L. A.

300
00:35:08,646 --> 00:35:10,605
Any of our people in the area?

301
00:35:10,606 --> 00:35:15,026
No one on the ground. Two A-1 Os
in the air. Williams and Mihradi.

302
00:35:15,027 --> 00:35:17,904
Send the birds in.

303
00:35:17,905 --> 00:35:20,948
Guide them to a safe area.

304
00:35:20,949 --> 00:35:24,577
Roger, Coyote 67 copies all.
Inbound to grid Lima-Alpha...

305
00:35:24,578 --> 00:35:26,620
...125793. Over.

306
00:35:26,621 --> 00:35:31,126
Copy that.
Roger, Wild Eagle. Solid copy.

307
00:36:26,762 --> 00:36:31,267
Hey, there's someone here.

308
00:36:31,433 --> 00:36:34,060
Get off him, get down!
Get down. Down!

309
00:36:34,061 --> 00:36:36,270
Drop your weapon!
Let me see your hands!

310
00:36:36,271 --> 00:36:37,980
Don't move.
That's it, drop it.

311
00:36:37,981 --> 00:36:42,318
Put it down!
What?

312
00:36:42,319 --> 00:36:45,362
- Is there a problem?
Hey, we saw your Resistance sign.

313
00:36:45,363 --> 00:36:48,574
The old lady put it there, not me.

314
00:36:48,575 --> 00:36:52,036
- What do you want?
- We're looking for fuel.

315
00:36:52,037 --> 00:36:54,413
The dark season's coming.

316
00:36:54,414 --> 00:36:56,748
We only got enough for ourselves.

317
00:36:56,749 --> 00:37:01,254
You point that gun at somebody,
you better be ready to pull the trigger.

318
00:37:02,630 --> 00:37:07,134
VIRGINIA:
Put your guns down, everyone.

319
00:37:08,594 --> 00:37:11,387
Look, we just came
to find the Resistance, that's all.

320
00:37:11,388 --> 00:37:13,097
The Resistance? Ha.

321
00:37:13,098 --> 00:37:17,060
What a joke.
Fighting those machines is impossible.

322
00:37:17,061 --> 00:37:19,061
We keep our heads down,
they ignore us.

323
00:37:19,062 --> 00:37:21,480
They'll come for you eventually.

324
00:37:21,481 --> 00:37:23,649
We help you, maybe they will.

325
00:37:23,650 --> 00:37:26,444
These people aren't going to help you.
Let's go.

326
00:37:26,445 --> 00:37:28,696
VIRGINIA:
You're not going anywhere.

327
00:37:28,697 --> 00:37:33,201
Not until this one
gets something to eat.

328
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:44,628
Bring me a basket.

329
00:37:44,629 --> 00:37:48,548
Here you go.

330
00:37:48,549 --> 00:37:53,053
Come on.
Help yourself. Eat up.

331
00:37:59,977 --> 00:38:03,854
Are you all right, son?

332
00:38:03,855 --> 00:38:05,481
It's our food.

333
00:38:05,482 --> 00:38:09,986
Our fuel.
It's not your choice to make!

334
00:38:43,810 --> 00:38:45,186
Are you okay?
- What?

335
00:38:45,187 --> 00:38:46,687
Are you okay?!

336
00:38:46,688 --> 00:38:49,940
Star. Star.
Star! Star!

337
00:38:49,941 --> 00:38:54,446
You! You brought them here!

338
00:38:54,779 --> 00:38:56,655
Hey!

339
00:38:56,656 --> 00:39:00,701
Stop! Stop!
Come on, quick!

340
00:39:00,702 --> 00:39:05,206
Hey.
Go! Go! Forget them! Go! Go!

341
00:39:08,209 --> 00:39:12,713
Go!

342
00:39:14,798 --> 00:39:19,303
Tunnels! Head for the tunnels!
Truck!

343
00:39:31,147 --> 00:39:35,192
Marcus. Marcus.

344
00:39:35,193 --> 00:39:39,697
We can't just run for it!

345
00:39:47,747 --> 00:39:52,251
Run!

346
00:40:25,783 --> 00:40:30,287
Shoot it!

347
00:40:31,831 --> 00:40:36,335
Go, go, go!

348
00:40:39,546 --> 00:40:42,340
It didn't work!

349
00:40:42,341 --> 00:40:46,845
Shit!

350
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:20,544
Ha. Hell, yeah!

351
00:41:22,587 --> 00:41:27,092
Oh.

352
00:41:35,433 --> 00:41:39,937
Moto-Terminators!

353
00:41:49,864 --> 00:41:54,368
Shoot that son of a bitch!

354
00:42:08,673 --> 00:42:13,178
Marcus, turn right up here.

355
00:42:23,020 --> 00:42:27,483
Hold on!

356
00:42:34,657 --> 00:42:39,119
Where's the other one?

357
00:42:52,132 --> 00:42:55,551
Get up here!

358
00:42:55,552 --> 00:43:00,014
Ugh. Ah!

359
00:43:00,348 --> 00:43:02,432
Come on.

360
00:43:02,433 --> 00:43:04,726
Star, give me the gun.

361
00:43:04,727 --> 00:43:08,271
I got it.

362
00:43:08,272 --> 00:43:12,735
Yeah!

363
00:43:19,074 --> 00:43:23,537
Hang on!

364
00:43:27,958 --> 00:43:32,462
- Drop the ball!
All right.

365
00:44:00,864 --> 00:44:05,368
Ah!

366
00:44:10,206 --> 00:44:14,711
Star, hold on!
Ah!

367
00:44:18,965 --> 00:44:23,469
Star! Star!
No!

368
00:45:00,880 --> 00:45:02,839
Kyle!
Marcus.

369
00:45:02,840 --> 00:45:07,345
Get back.

370
00:45:09,138 --> 00:45:13,391
Marcus! Marcus!

371
00:45:13,392 --> 00:45:16,436
Ah!

372
00:45:16,437 --> 00:45:18,312
MAN
Got eyes on two targets.

373
00:45:18,313 --> 00:45:21,023
BLAIR
We've got two bogeys at 270 degrees.

374
00:45:21,024 --> 00:45:25,529
They've never come this deep before.
They're looking for something.

375
00:45:30,325 --> 00:45:34,829
BLAIR
H. K. is down.

376
00:45:47,633 --> 00:45:49,552
MAN
We've got an H. K. pushing our six.

377
00:45:49,553 --> 00:45:54,056
BLAIR Abort run.
MAN Breaking off

378
00:45:58,811 --> 00:46:03,315
Evasive maneuvers, now!

379
00:46:05,984 --> 00:46:10,488
Taking fire. I'm hit. Port-side damage.

380
00:46:14,242 --> 00:46:18,746
It's got a lock on you. Break off.

381
00:46:19,288 --> 00:46:23,793
- Eject, Williams, eject!
Punching out.

382
00:46:40,017 --> 00:46:43,769
Prisoner transport
headed northwest...

383
00:46:43,770 --> 00:46:48,275
...bearing 289 toward San Francisco.

384
00:46:48,650 --> 00:46:51,402
Let's test the signal...

385
00:46:51,403 --> 00:46:55,907
...and pray it works.

386
00:47:32,233 --> 00:47:36,738
Ah.

387
00:47:48,499 --> 00:47:49,707
Ugh.

388
00:47:49,708 --> 00:47:51,501
You okay?

389
00:47:51,502 --> 00:47:56,006
Get my knife. It's in my left boot.

390
00:48:01,762 --> 00:48:03,471
What's your name?

391
00:48:03,472 --> 00:48:07,099
Blair Williams.

392
00:48:07,100 --> 00:48:11,604
What's yours?

393
00:48:12,939 --> 00:48:15,107
Name's Marcus.

394
00:48:15,108 --> 00:48:19,612
You can let me down now, Marcus.

395
00:48:25,701 --> 00:48:30,372
- That thing, where'd it go?
- The transport? Skynet.

396
00:48:30,539 --> 00:48:33,875
- Where the hell are you going?
- After it.

397
00:48:33,876 --> 00:48:37,670
I hate to break it to you,
but if you have friends on that thing...

398
00:48:37,671 --> 00:48:41,799
...they're as good as dead. And same
as you, if you walk in that direction.

399
00:48:41,800 --> 00:48:44,802
Yeah, I've been dead a while
and I'm getting used to it.

400
00:48:44,803 --> 00:48:46,929
Why don't you come with me
to my base?

401
00:48:46,930 --> 00:48:51,434
Connor might know a way.

402
00:48:52,394 --> 00:48:54,978
If you have a problem
with the machines...

403
00:48:54,979 --> 00:48:59,399
...he's definitely the guy
you wanna talk to.

404
00:48:59,400 --> 00:49:03,278
- How far is your base?
- Should be one or two days' hike.

405
00:49:03,279 --> 00:49:07,783
And it's that way.

406
00:49:29,596 --> 00:49:34,099
What are you saying? Speak English!

407
00:49:34,100 --> 00:49:39,105
NAIMA: I was telling him it is not true
about the machines killing us.

408
00:49:39,272 --> 00:49:42,315
HIDEKl: They're gonna kill us.
They're gonna kill everyone.

409
00:49:42,316 --> 00:49:44,818
We're on the way
to the slaughterhouse!

410
00:49:44,819 --> 00:49:48,822
Calm down. You're not helping.

411
00:49:48,823 --> 00:49:53,369
The most important thing we can do
right now is stay alive.

412
00:49:53,535 --> 00:49:56,329
In here and in here.

413
00:49:56,330 --> 00:50:00,834
All right? Just stay alive.

414
00:50:14,848 --> 00:50:19,352
Over there.

415
00:50:23,231 --> 00:50:27,735
Find something we can burn.
We'll be at my base tomorrow.

416
00:50:30,154 --> 00:50:33,573
Are you hurt?

417
00:50:33,574 --> 00:50:38,078
I'm fine.

418
00:51:46,894 --> 00:51:51,357
What do you got there?

419
00:51:51,649 --> 00:51:54,025
Just some antibiotics.

420
00:51:54,026 --> 00:51:57,278
Antibiotics are hard
to come by these days.

421
00:51:57,279 --> 00:52:01,449
Listen. I don't have much, but
you're welcome to whatever you need.

422
00:52:01,450 --> 00:52:04,952
We've been watching you.

423
00:52:04,953 --> 00:52:08,205
You looking for this?

424
00:52:08,206 --> 00:52:11,291
Come on, guys.
The machines are the enemy.

425
00:52:11,292 --> 00:52:13,961
- We're all on the same side.
No, no.

426
00:52:13,962 --> 00:52:16,547
You see,
I got a couple friends on my side.

427
00:52:16,548 --> 00:52:21,010
Maybe they can carry you home
when I'm done with you.

428
00:52:22,678 --> 00:52:26,389
You might want to chamber a round.

429
00:52:26,390 --> 00:52:30,853
Oh, no.
No.

430
00:52:31,270 --> 00:52:35,774
We done caught us a donkey!
Been waiting for you.

431
00:52:54,542 --> 00:52:59,047
Unh! Richter!

432
00:53:11,517 --> 00:53:16,021
Killing me ain't gonna win this war!

433
00:53:18,816 --> 00:53:23,320
Ah!

434
00:54:00,230 --> 00:54:04,735
Thinking about your past?

435
00:54:11,116 --> 00:54:15,620
You know what I've learned, Marcus?

436
00:54:16,287 --> 00:54:20,792
Is you can focus on what is lost...

437
00:54:22,502 --> 00:54:27,006
...or you can fight for what is left.

438
00:54:38,350 --> 00:54:42,854
WHISPERS]
I'm a little cold.

439
00:54:49,194 --> 00:54:53,698
Relax.

440
00:54:53,865 --> 00:54:58,369
I just want some body heat.

441
00:55:02,206 --> 00:55:06,543
You have a strong heart.

442
00:55:06,544 --> 00:55:11,048
God, I love that sound.

443
00:55:15,552 --> 00:55:20,057
Thank you for saving me back there.

444
00:55:20,724 --> 00:55:25,228
I don't meet a lot of good guys
these days.

445
00:55:25,395 --> 00:55:29,899
I'm not a good guy.

446
00:55:33,570 --> 00:55:36,071
You are.

447
00:55:36,072 --> 00:55:40,576
You just don't know it yet.

448
00:55:47,458 --> 00:55:51,962
Do you think people deserve
a second chance?

449
00:55:53,756 --> 00:55:58,260
Yeah, I do.

450
00:55:59,970 --> 00:56:04,808
This is it. Skynet's valley of death.
We never been this deep before.

451
00:56:04,975 --> 00:56:08,060
We gotta be sure the signal works
in their territory...

452
00:56:08,061 --> 00:56:12,565
...on the bigger machines.

453
00:56:20,281 --> 00:56:24,785
That'll bring them in.

454
00:56:39,216 --> 00:56:43,720
H. K. incoming.

455
00:57:02,822 --> 00:57:07,326
Turn it up!

456
00:57:16,960 --> 00:57:21,465
Oh...

457
00:57:26,845 --> 00:57:31,349
It works, man.
The signal works. It's beautiful.

458
00:57:42,276 --> 00:57:43,610
Commander Ashdown's on.

459
00:57:43,611 --> 00:57:45,278
Connor, tell me it works.

460
00:57:45,279 --> 00:57:48,323
It works. That is affirmative.
The signal works.

461
00:57:48,324 --> 00:57:52,368
Good. The attack commences
tomorrow at 0400, worldwide.

462
00:57:52,369 --> 00:57:56,039
Your unit will be in support
of the bombing of Skynet Central.

463
00:57:56,040 --> 00:57:58,541
What is the extraction plan
for the prisoners?

464
00:57:58,542 --> 00:58:00,877
Extraction plan?
There is no extraction plan.

465
00:58:00,878 --> 00:58:05,339
- We're gonna level the place.
- Negative. I told you...

466
00:58:05,340 --> 00:58:09,844
...Skynet Central
is filled with human prisoners!

467
00:58:10,178 --> 00:58:11,512
This is war, Connor.

468
00:58:11,513 --> 00:58:16,017
Leadership has its costs.
You, above all, should know that.

469
00:58:17,352 --> 00:58:19,686
Ashdown, come in!

470
00:58:19,687 --> 00:58:21,730
Ashdown, Connor.

471
00:58:21,731 --> 00:58:26,235
Ashdown, come-Damn him!

472
00:58:37,454 --> 00:58:41,959
Star! Get back! Get back!

473
00:58:47,339 --> 00:58:51,843
You have to calm down now.

474
00:59:04,230 --> 00:59:08,734
I gotta get out!
I gotta get out of here!

475
00:59:23,665 --> 00:59:24,999
Blair?

476
00:59:25,000 --> 00:59:29,211
What?

477
00:59:29,212 --> 00:59:32,631
This is us. The mines are magnetic.

478
00:59:32,632 --> 00:59:37,136
If we head due west
at this point of entry, we're good.

479
00:59:38,179 --> 00:59:42,683
I'll go first.

480
01:00:08,750 --> 01:00:13,254
Let's go, Marcus. I'm starving.

481
01:00:20,011 --> 01:00:22,095
PRIEST
For thou art with me.

482
01:00:22,096 --> 01:00:25,724
Thy rod and thy staff,
they comfort me.

483
01:00:25,725 --> 01:00:29,352
Father.

484
01:00:29,353 --> 01:00:32,230
SERENA
This is the beginning...

485
01:00:32,231 --> 01:00:36,026
...of something wonderful.

486
01:00:36,068 --> 01:00:37,361
Son of a bitch is heavy.

487
01:00:37,362 --> 01:00:39,863
What have we got?
He stepped on a land mine.

488
01:00:39,905 --> 01:00:41,906
Start a large-bore IV.

489
01:00:41,907 --> 01:00:43,867
- Keep it open. More morphine.
- I'm okay.

490
01:00:43,909 --> 01:00:48,371
- What's his name?
- Marcus.

491
01:00:48,538 --> 01:00:52,250
- He's got a prosthetic limb?
- What?

492
01:00:52,292 --> 01:00:56,754
Okay, pulse is good.
Let's see what we've got.

493
01:01:01,092 --> 01:01:05,554
Barnes.

494
01:01:07,932 --> 01:01:12,394
The devil's hands have been busy.

495
01:01:12,603 --> 01:01:14,145
What is it?

496
01:01:14,146 --> 01:01:18,566
It's real fesh and blood,
though it seems to heal itself quickly.

497
01:01:18,567 --> 01:01:22,987
The heart is human
and very powerful.

498
01:01:22,988 --> 01:01:25,322
The brain, too,
but with a chip interface.

499
01:01:25,323 --> 01:01:28,993
What have you done to me?
- It has a hybrid nervous system.

500
01:01:28,994 --> 01:01:32,121
One human cortex, one machine.

501
01:01:32,122 --> 01:01:35,082
Blair, what have they done?

502
01:01:35,083 --> 01:01:37,626
Who built you?

503
01:01:37,627 --> 01:01:42,090
My name is Marcus Wright.

504
01:01:42,131 --> 01:01:44,299
You think you're human?

505
01:01:44,300 --> 01:01:48,804
I am human.

506
01:02:11,493 --> 01:02:14,745
MARCUS
No!

507
01:02:14,746 --> 01:02:19,250
No!

508
01:02:20,501 --> 01:02:23,211
Where were you manufactured?

509
01:02:23,212 --> 01:02:25,922
I was born...

510
01:02:25,923 --> 01:02:29,509
...August 22, 1975.

511
01:02:29,510 --> 01:02:34,014
No.

512
01:02:40,354 --> 01:02:43,064
I know you.

513
01:02:43,065 --> 01:02:47,026
I heard your voice on the radio.

514
01:02:47,027 --> 01:02:51,030
- You're John Connor.
Of course you know me.

515
01:02:51,031 --> 01:02:54,032
You were sent here to kill me.

516
01:02:54,033 --> 01:02:56,159
Kill the leadership.

517
01:02:56,160 --> 01:02:59,371
- I don't know what you're talking about.
- Then why are you here?

518
01:02:59,372 --> 01:03:03,876
Blair said you'd help me
find who I'm looking for.

519
01:03:05,670 --> 01:03:10,174
- Now, let me down.
- If I let you down...

520
01:03:10,424 --> 01:03:12,884
...you'll kill everyone in this room.

521
01:03:12,885 --> 01:03:17,389
Just you, Connor.
Because I don't give a shit about you.

522
01:03:17,556 --> 01:03:19,724
I didn't know your name
till two days ago.

523
01:03:19,725 --> 01:03:24,229
No.

524
01:03:24,980 --> 01:03:27,565
You and me...

525
01:03:27,566 --> 01:03:32,946
...we've been at war
since before either of us even existed.

526
01:03:33,822 --> 01:03:38,326
You tried killing my mother,
Sarah Connor.

527
01:03:38,493 --> 01:03:42,746
You killed my father, Kyle Reese.

528
01:03:42,747 --> 01:03:46,458
You will not kill me.

529
01:03:46,459 --> 01:03:52,423
Kyle Reese is on a transporter
heading for Skynet.

530
01:03:53,257 --> 01:03:55,925
If I wanted to kill him...

531
01:03:55,926 --> 01:04:00,430
...I'd have done him in L. A.

532
01:04:04,267 --> 01:04:06,018
Where'd you find that thing?

533
01:04:06,019 --> 01:04:09,104
You sent Mihradi and me
to provide cover for some civilians.

534
01:04:09,105 --> 01:04:12,649
- He was one of them.
- Was there a teenage boy?

535
01:04:12,650 --> 01:04:16,320
I don't know. They were taken into
a transport. He was the only one left.

536
01:04:16,321 --> 01:04:19,281
Not "he, " Blair. "It."

537
01:04:19,282 --> 01:04:22,117
It was the only one left.
Don't be naÏve.

538
01:04:22,118 --> 01:04:26,622
It saved my life.

539
01:04:27,289 --> 01:04:30,291
Kate, what's gonna happen to him?

540
01:04:30,292 --> 01:04:32,502
Disassembled.

541
01:04:32,503 --> 01:04:37,007
- You mean killed.
- It may have information on Skynet.

542
01:04:38,342 --> 01:04:42,888
I know he's not the enemy. I've been
shot at by the enemy. That's not him.

543
01:04:43,055 --> 01:04:47,559
That machine saved you
only to gain access to kill all of us.

544
01:05:27,681 --> 01:05:32,185
We're gonna be okay. Don't worry.

545
01:05:47,199 --> 01:05:51,704
For my brother.

546
01:05:59,670 --> 01:06:04,174
No!

547
01:06:08,053 --> 01:06:10,137
Connor wants to see you.

548
01:06:10,138 --> 01:06:12,222
What for?

549
01:06:12,223 --> 01:06:16,728
Like he's gonna tell me, Barnes.

550
01:06:16,895 --> 01:06:21,399
Let me see that.

551
01:06:24,819 --> 01:06:27,028
Want me to tell Connor
you're not coming?

552
01:06:27,029 --> 01:06:31,534
No.

553
01:06:32,743 --> 01:06:37,247
Watch him.

554
01:07:01,938 --> 01:07:04,773
I told you everything I know, John.

555
01:07:04,774 --> 01:07:07,901
Skynet is ruthless
and unpredictable.

556
01:07:07,902 --> 01:07:11,237
They wilI use the best part of you
against yourself.

557
01:07:11,238 --> 01:07:15,158
And they will have methods
I can't imagine or predict...

558
01:07:15,159 --> 01:07:17,785
...that I can't help you with.

559
01:07:17,786 --> 01:07:22,791
And when you're unsure, well,
just always follow your heart, John.

560
01:07:22,958 --> 01:07:27,462
I love you. Goodbye.

561
01:07:28,129 --> 01:07:30,923
There's nothing
about machines with organs.

562
01:07:30,924 --> 01:07:35,385
That thing in there...

563
01:07:35,386 --> 01:07:37,638
I thought I knew our enemy.

564
01:07:37,639 --> 01:07:42,143
But that thing, that makes me feel
like I know nothing.

565
01:07:43,519 --> 01:07:47,939
I looked in its eyes, and it believes,
absolutely believes...

566
01:07:47,940 --> 01:07:49,399
...that it is human.

567
01:07:49,400 --> 01:07:52,902
It believes everything that it says.

568
01:07:52,903 --> 01:07:55,154
And it is telling me...

569
01:07:55,155 --> 01:07:58,741
...that Kyle Reese is in Skynet.

570
01:07:58,742 --> 01:08:00,159
If that is true...

571
01:08:00,160 --> 01:08:05,582
...then Command is about to bomb my
father and the rest of those prisoners...

572
01:08:05,749 --> 01:08:10,253
...and I cannot stop them.

573
01:08:15,425 --> 01:08:18,135
Thank you.

574
01:08:18,136 --> 01:08:21,763
Come in.

575
01:08:21,764 --> 01:08:26,269
What's up?
Blair said you needed me.

576
01:08:45,120 --> 01:08:47,997
Get in.

577
01:08:47,998 --> 01:08:52,502
Get him.

578
01:08:56,589 --> 01:09:00,884
Barnes. What about Blair?
- She made her choice.

579
01:09:00,885 --> 01:09:05,389
Get down!

580
01:09:14,606 --> 01:09:19,111
Let's move.

581
01:09:28,203 --> 01:09:31,163
Get some light out there!
We're back in the minefield.

582
01:09:31,164 --> 01:09:35,668
I have a plan.

583
01:09:47,138 --> 01:09:51,642
Let's run!
There they go, they're on the move.

584
01:09:55,896 --> 01:09:58,148
Blair, you okay?
Yeah, I'm okay!

585
01:09:58,190 --> 01:10:01,109
I can't see back!
There they are!

586
01:10:01,151 --> 01:10:05,614
Run! Go!

587
01:10:13,872 --> 01:10:16,415
Now what?

588
01:10:16,416 --> 01:10:19,334
My plan stopped at the jeep.

589
01:10:19,335 --> 01:10:23,798
Sniper Team 1, do you have a shot?

590
01:10:28,719 --> 01:10:33,182
I'll draw the fire.
You take out the light.

591
01:10:40,647 --> 01:10:45,110
I got a target!

592
01:10:46,862 --> 01:10:51,324
Go! Now! Keep your head down!
Keep your head down!

593
01:10:51,366 --> 01:10:54,201
- Go, go, go!
Go, go, go!

594
01:10:54,202 --> 01:10:58,706
Go! Go, keep running!

595
01:11:00,792 --> 01:11:05,296
Come on! Come on!

596
01:11:08,257 --> 01:11:12,761
- You all right?
- Let's get you out of here.

597
01:11:16,807 --> 01:11:21,311
There they are!

598
01:11:35,950 --> 01:11:40,455
Stay on the ground!
Stay on the ground!

599
01:11:40,747 --> 01:11:42,747
MAN 2 You come
on straight down. I'm going in.

600
01:11:42,748 --> 01:11:45,709
Do not move!
Keep your eye on him!

601
01:11:45,710 --> 01:11:50,214
Flip him!

602
01:12:28,876 --> 01:12:32,462
MAN Iron Gator, this is
Scarface 51. We have eyes on the machine.

603
01:12:32,463 --> 01:12:36,967
Contact initiated.

604
01:12:47,978 --> 01:12:52,482
Take my gun!

605
01:13:22,928 --> 01:13:27,432
Check the river.

606
01:13:40,528 --> 01:13:45,032
You see him?

607
01:14:08,221 --> 01:14:11,640
Hydraulics are out!

608
01:14:11,641 --> 01:14:16,145
Ahh!

609
01:14:21,776 --> 01:14:26,280
Give me your hand!
Give me your hand!

610
01:15:13,158 --> 01:15:17,120
- They know you, even if you don't.
- Enough!

611
01:15:17,121 --> 01:15:19,038
That gun ain't gonna stop shit!

612
01:15:19,039 --> 01:15:22,124
Nobody's shot you in the heart,
and I see that thing beating!

613
01:15:22,125 --> 01:15:24,126
Kyle Reese.

614
01:15:24,127 --> 01:15:27,630
He's in Skynet.
You do that, he's dead.

615
01:15:27,631 --> 01:15:30,799
I can get you in.

616
01:15:30,800 --> 01:15:35,305
How?

617
01:15:38,474 --> 01:15:41,810
Look at me.

618
01:15:41,811 --> 01:15:45,981
That's why I don't trust you.

619
01:15:45,982 --> 01:15:50,486
I'm the only hope you have.

620
01:15:52,029 --> 01:15:56,324
I need to find who did this to me.

621
01:15:56,325 --> 01:15:58,701
So do you.

622
01:15:58,702 --> 01:16:03,206
SOLDIER:
Connor!

623
01:16:06,585 --> 01:16:09,837
Make your choice.

624
01:16:09,838 --> 01:16:14,174
You get me in.

625
01:16:14,175 --> 01:16:18,680
You tell me where I can find
Kyle Reese.

626
01:16:20,264 --> 01:16:22,182
Yeah?

627
01:16:22,183 --> 01:16:26,687
I will.

628
01:16:29,523 --> 01:16:34,278
Contact me on that.
Let me know he's still alive.

629
01:16:39,992 --> 01:16:42,076
What are you?

630
01:16:42,077 --> 01:16:46,581
I don't know.

631
01:16:50,543 --> 01:16:55,048
SOLDIER:
He's over here!

632
01:16:56,007 --> 01:16:58,216
You all right?

633
01:16:58,217 --> 01:17:01,219
Any sign of him?

634
01:17:01,220 --> 01:17:05,725
He's gone.

635
01:17:10,438 --> 01:17:13,398
Why'd you do it?

636
01:17:13,399 --> 01:17:15,400
I saw a man...

637
01:17:15,401 --> 01:17:19,905
...not a machine.

638
01:17:25,410 --> 01:17:27,119
How's that leg?

639
01:17:27,120 --> 01:17:31,624
- I'll live.
- Let her go!

640
01:17:39,590 --> 01:17:43,635
COMMS OFFICER:
Connor? Command for you.

641
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:46,346
- This is Connor.
- Connor, are your men ready?

642
01:17:46,347 --> 01:17:48,598
Negative. Nobody is ready.

643
01:17:48,599 --> 01:17:53,437
We are not, you are not. We must abort
the attack. The game has changed.

644
01:17:53,604 --> 01:17:57,148
What are you talking about? All
elements are past their release points.

645
01:17:57,149 --> 01:17:58,941
They're in assault position.

646
01:17:58,942 --> 01:18:02,778
Then delay the attack. At least,
delay the attack. I have a chance...

647
01:18:02,779 --> 01:18:06,699
...to infiltrate Skynet and rescue those
prisoners. Give me that opportunity.

648
01:18:06,700 --> 01:18:10,452
No, absolutely not! This is not
the time for a rescue mission!

649
01:18:10,453 --> 01:18:13,122
What you ask for will undermine
the whole operation.

650
01:18:13,123 --> 01:18:16,291
Skynet has Kyle Reese.

651
01:18:16,292 --> 01:18:18,961
- Then that is his fate.
- It's our fate.

652
01:18:18,962 --> 01:18:21,963
I have to save him. He is the key.

653
01:18:21,964 --> 01:18:27,053
The key to the future, to the past.
Without him, we lose everything.

654
01:18:27,219 --> 01:18:29,220
No, you stay the course!

655
01:18:29,221 --> 01:18:33,726
If we stay the course, we are dead!
We are all dead!

656
01:18:34,727 --> 01:18:36,686
As of this moment, soldier...

657
01:18:36,687 --> 01:18:38,647
...you are relieved of your command.

658
01:18:38,648 --> 01:18:43,151
You are no longer a part
of this Resistance.

659
01:18:49,199 --> 01:18:51,700
I didn't catch that last statement.

660
01:18:51,701 --> 01:18:56,206
Neither did I.

661
01:18:56,414 --> 01:18:57,873
This is John Connor.

662
01:18:57,874 --> 01:19:02,003
If you're listening to this,
you are the Resistance.

663
01:19:02,044 --> 01:19:05,797
Listen carefully.
If we attack tonight...

664
01:19:05,798 --> 01:19:08,509
...our humanity is lost.

665
01:19:08,551 --> 01:19:12,555
I once knew a woman who told people
to fear the future...

666
01:19:12,596 --> 01:19:16,891
...that the end was coming,
that all would be lost.

667
01:19:16,892 --> 01:19:22,272
Nobody wanted to hear her truths.
Society locked her away.

668
01:19:22,439 --> 01:19:26,902
That woman was Sarah Connor,
my mother.

669
01:19:27,152 --> 01:19:31,614
Now we know that what she
predicted has all come to pass.

670
01:19:31,740 --> 01:19:33,824
Command wants us
to fight like machines.

671
01:19:33,825 --> 01:19:37,077
They want us
to make cold, calculated decisions.

672
01:19:37,078 --> 01:19:39,413
But we are not machines!

673
01:19:39,414 --> 01:19:44,210
And if we behave like them,
then what is the point in winning?

674
01:19:44,794 --> 01:19:49,256
Command is going to ask you
to attack Skynet.

675
01:19:49,840 --> 01:19:54,345
I am asking you not to.

676
01:19:54,720 --> 01:19:59,433
If even one bomb drops on Skynet
before sunrise...

677
01:19:59,600 --> 01:20:02,685
...our future will be lost.

678
01:20:02,686 --> 01:20:07,190
So please, stand down.
Give me the time...

679
01:20:07,566 --> 01:20:10,734
...to protect our future that all of us...

680
01:20:10,735 --> 01:20:15,072
...are fighting for.

681
01:20:15,073 --> 01:20:19,577
This is John Connor.

682
01:20:41,056 --> 01:20:45,560
What should I tell your men
when they find out you're gone?

683
01:20:48,438 --> 01:20:52,942
I'll be back.

684
01:22:43,256 --> 01:22:47,761
I'm coming for you.

685
01:23:30,885 --> 01:23:35,390
Come on, Marcus.

686
01:24:32,278 --> 01:24:36,782
Kyle.

687
01:24:43,664 --> 01:24:48,168
Okay.

688
01:26:22,175 --> 01:26:24,801
Signal broadcasting
at full strength, sir.

689
01:26:24,802 --> 01:26:29,598
- Good. Commence bombing of Skynet.
SOLDIER: We have a green light to attack.

690
01:26:29,765 --> 01:26:32,475
This is Bakersfield.
That's a no-go on your last. Out.

691
01:26:32,476 --> 01:26:34,227
Eugene, standing down.

692
01:26:34,228 --> 01:26:35,813
This is Reno. Negative on your last.

693
01:26:35,814 --> 01:26:38,940
SOLDIER: Eugene, Reno, Bakersfield.
They're all standing down.

694
01:26:38,941 --> 01:26:43,445
They will not attack
unless Connor gives the order.

695
01:27:09,970 --> 01:27:11,846
Kyle Reese?

696
01:27:11,847 --> 01:27:16,352
Get to the transport! Go!
Is Kyle Reese here?

697
01:27:36,037 --> 01:27:38,288
Welcome home, Marcus.

698
01:27:38,289 --> 01:27:40,332
We knew you'd be back.

699
01:27:40,333 --> 01:27:44,085
After all, it was programmed in you.

700
01:27:44,086 --> 01:27:48,591
Oh. And you executed
that programming beautifully.

701
01:27:48,674 --> 01:27:50,508
What am I?

702
01:27:50,509 --> 01:27:55,014
You are an infiltration prototype.
The only one of your kind.

703
01:27:55,055 --> 01:27:59,768
We resurrected you, advanced
Cyberdyne's work, amended it.

704
01:27:59,935 --> 01:28:01,477
You're dead.

705
01:28:01,478 --> 01:28:06,608
Calculations confirm Serena Kogan's
face is the easiest for you to process.

706
01:28:06,775 --> 01:28:11,279
We can be others if you wish.

707
01:28:11,404 --> 01:28:14,657
Marcus, what else could you be...

708
01:28:14,699 --> 01:28:16,909
...if not machine?

709
01:28:16,910 --> 01:28:18,995
A man.

710
01:28:19,037 --> 01:28:21,456
The human condition
no longer applies to you.

711
01:28:21,497 --> 01:28:23,833
Accept what you already know.

712
01:28:23,875 --> 01:28:27,419
That you were made
to serve a purpose.

713
01:28:27,420 --> 01:28:31,882
To achieve what no other machine
has achieved before.

714
01:28:32,174 --> 01:28:38,722
To infiltrate, find a target, and then
bring that target back home to us.

715
01:28:40,891 --> 01:28:45,186
We've been at war since
before either of us even existed.

716
01:28:45,187 --> 01:28:48,898
You tried killing my mother,
Sarah Connor.

717
01:28:48,899 --> 01:28:51,400
You get me in.

718
01:28:51,401 --> 01:28:53,944
You tell me
where I can find Kyle Reese.

719
01:28:53,945 --> 01:28:58,408
- Yeah?
I will.

720
01:29:00,493 --> 01:29:04,287
Kyle Reese! Kyle Reese!
Move! Move!

721
01:29:04,288 --> 01:29:06,581
Kyle Reese!

722
01:29:06,582 --> 01:29:08,583
Get to the transports!

723
01:29:08,584 --> 01:29:13,088
- Kyle Reese?
- No.

724
01:29:16,592 --> 01:29:18,885
You! Move!

725
01:29:18,886 --> 01:29:23,306
In times of desperation, people will
believe what they want to believe.

726
01:29:23,307 --> 01:29:27,601
And so, we gave them
what they wanted to believe.

727
01:29:27,602 --> 01:29:31,605
A trick, in the form of a signal the
Resistance thought would win the war.

728
01:29:31,606 --> 01:29:34,983
And they were right,
it will end this war.

729
01:29:34,984 --> 01:29:38,612
Except that it is the Resistance
that will be terminated.

730
01:29:38,613 --> 01:29:43,117
Not Skynet.

731
01:29:46,912 --> 01:29:49,914
Get the attack
on Skynet Central back online.

732
01:29:49,915 --> 01:29:52,876
I want our aircraft in the sky
immediately.

733
01:29:52,877 --> 01:29:56,129
Sir. Sir, we've got a bogey
with a very large radar signature...

734
01:29:56,130 --> 01:30:00,634
...closing in on our position.

735
01:30:08,767 --> 01:30:13,271
Losenko?

736
01:30:15,607 --> 01:30:18,358
We have destroyed ourselves.

737
01:30:18,359 --> 01:30:22,864
Skynet tracked our signal.
We led them straight to us.

738
01:30:35,334 --> 01:30:39,212
Our best machines had failed
time and again to complete a mission.

739
01:30:39,213 --> 01:30:43,215
Something was missing.
We had to think. Radically.

740
01:30:43,216 --> 01:30:48,096
And so we made you. ye created
the perfect infiltration machine.

741
01:30:49,556 --> 01:30:51,265
You, Marcus.

742
01:30:51,266 --> 01:30:55,770
You did what Skynet has failed to do
for so many years.

743
01:30:55,937 --> 01:31:00,441
You killed John Connor.

744
01:31:58,288 --> 01:32:00,831
Kyle!

745
01:32:00,832 --> 01:32:05,337
Hey!

746
01:32:11,509 --> 01:32:14,011
Don't fight, Marcus.

747
01:32:14,012 --> 01:32:16,847
Remember what you are.

748
01:32:16,848 --> 01:32:21,352
I know what I am.

749
01:32:31,820 --> 01:32:33,488
I'm better this way.

750
01:32:33,489 --> 01:32:36,574
You will not be given
a second chance.

751
01:32:36,575 --> 01:32:41,079
- You cannot save John Connor.
- Watch me.

752
01:33:10,524 --> 01:33:12,609
Got a message from Connor.

753
01:33:12,610 --> 01:33:16,904
He's in Skynet, needs air support.

754
01:33:16,905 --> 01:33:21,410
Let's go. Scramble aircraft!

755
01:33:22,744 --> 01:33:27,249
Star! Star, go!

756
01:33:33,713 --> 01:33:35,047
Star!

757
01:33:35,048 --> 01:33:39,552
Star! Star! Come on. Come on.

758
01:33:59,863 --> 01:34:04,368
- What's your name?
- Kyle Reese.

759
01:34:08,371 --> 01:34:12,876
Stay with me.

760
01:34:29,934 --> 01:34:31,534
Back!

761
01:34:46,658 --> 01:34:51,162
Come on, Star, move! Move!

762
01:35:16,395 --> 01:35:18,896
T-800s.

763
01:35:18,897 --> 01:35:23,402
There's so many of them.

764
01:35:40,293 --> 01:35:44,797
Careful.

765
01:35:46,090 --> 01:35:48,675
- What are these?
Fuel cells.

766
01:35:48,676 --> 01:35:53,180
Life source for the T-800.

767
01:35:54,014 --> 01:35:56,349
Nuclear.

768
01:35:56,350 --> 01:36:00,603
Enough to level this place.

769
01:36:00,604 --> 01:36:03,105
Cover us.

770
01:36:03,106 --> 01:36:07,611
Get ready.

771
01:36:08,695 --> 01:36:13,199
This is it.

772
01:36:34,261 --> 01:36:36,888
Run!

773
01:36:36,889 --> 01:36:40,224
Star, come on! Let's go!

774
01:36:40,225 --> 01:36:44,730
Get in.

775
01:36:44,980 --> 01:36:49,484
Come on!

776
01:36:49,985 --> 01:36:54,489
We gotta get to the transport.

777
01:36:57,575 --> 01:36:59,660
Where are you going?
- I gotta end this.

778
01:36:59,661 --> 01:37:01,578
No, no. I'm not gonna leave you!

779
01:37:01,579 --> 01:37:05,332
- You didn't.
- Who are you?

780
01:37:05,333 --> 01:37:09,837
John Connor.

781
01:40:15,181 --> 01:40:18,809
Hey! Hey, John Connor's in there.
He's still in there.

782
01:40:18,810 --> 01:40:20,894
Chris, she's hypovolemic,
start a line!

783
01:40:20,895 --> 01:40:23,605
- What?
- John Connor's in there.

784
01:40:23,606 --> 01:40:28,110
Come with me.

785
01:40:43,834 --> 01:40:48,338
Connor!

786
01:40:49,214 --> 01:40:51,924
Connor, help!

787
01:40:51,925 --> 01:40:54,718
Help!

788
01:40:54,719 --> 01:40:59,223
Connor, it's Kyle. Help!

789
01:41:55,611 --> 01:42:00,115
Do it! You son of a bitch!

790
01:42:26,974 --> 01:42:28,974
Come on!

791
01:43:51,555 --> 01:43:56,060
Let's get out of here.

792
01:44:11,116 --> 01:44:15,620
John.

793
01:44:17,247 --> 01:44:22,084
We can't make it back to base.
Set this down in the nearest safe zone.

794
01:44:28,090 --> 01:44:31,634
Medevac, urgent.
Severe chest trauma.

795
01:44:31,635 --> 01:44:36,265
Call the surgical team.
Remarks: it's Connor.

796
01:45:53,672 --> 01:45:58,177
How long?

797
01:45:58,886 --> 01:46:02,722
His heart...

798
01:46:02,723 --> 01:46:04,056
...can't take it.

799
01:46:04,057 --> 01:46:07,601
It's gonna be okay.
It's gonna be okay, Kate.

800
01:46:07,602 --> 01:46:12,107
Kyle?

801
01:46:22,617 --> 01:46:27,121
Take it.

802
01:46:43,679 --> 01:46:48,141
You earned it.

803
01:47:04,115 --> 01:47:08,577
Kate?

804
01:47:11,789 --> 01:47:14,290
Take mine.

805
01:47:14,291 --> 01:47:18,754
Marcus...

806
01:47:19,463 --> 01:47:23,925
Everybody deserves
a second chance.

807
01:47:25,469 --> 01:47:29,931
This is mine.

808
01:48:24,400 --> 01:48:28,737
What is it that makes us human?

809
01:48:28,738 --> 01:48:32,907
It's not something
you can program.

810
01:48:32,908 --> 01:48:37,370
You can't put it into a chip.

811
01:48:37,371 --> 01:48:40,706
It's the strength of the human heart.

812
01:48:40,707 --> 01:48:45,212
The difference between us
and machines.

813
01:49:03,437 --> 01:49:08,734
There is a storm on the horizon.
A time of hardship and pain.

814
01:49:08,901 --> 01:49:14,073
This battle has been won, but the war
against the machines rages on.

815
01:49:14,239 --> 01:49:17,408
Skynet's global network
remains strong.

816
01:49:17,409 --> 01:49:20,119
But we will not quit...

817
01:49:20,120 --> 01:49:22,413
...until all of it is destroyed.

818
01:49:22,414 --> 01:49:28,044
This is John Connor.
There is no fate but what we make.

